diff --git a/Phase-Aware-Tracking.md b/Phase-Aware-Tracking.md
index af0fe72..804df5d 100644
--- a/Phase-Aware-Tracking.md
+++ b/Phase-Aware-Tracking.md
@@ -256,6 +256,11 @@ Phase-aware tracking works independently from [[Diagram Customisation › Setup
 
 You can use both together: suppress noisy setup database calls (`TrackDuringSetup = false` on the DB extension) while still showing setup HTTP calls in a partition (`SeparateSetup = true`).
 
+A call's phase does not draw the partition on its own: the partition is drawn at the Setup/Action boundary. For
+an ingested run, `kronikol ingest --phase-from-steps` gives each call the phase of its step, and
+`--separate-setup` draws the partition, from the steps or from the calls' phases (4.1.0+; see
+[[Ingesting External Captures › The Setup partition|Ingesting-External-Captures#the-setup-partition-410]]).
+
